WEBVTT

00:00.680 --> 00:03.940
<b>A peaceful existence——</b>

00:06.730 --> 00:08.030
The usual.

00:08.030 --> 00:09.020
Sure thing.

00:09.300 --> 00:10.750
One taco roll.

00:11.320 --> 00:14.090
Don't you ever get bored of that?

00:14.700 --> 00:17.900
And you always breathe the same air.

00:17.900 --> 00:19.080
Have you ever gotten bored of it?

00:21.190 --> 00:21.970
Here.

00:21.970 --> 00:23.830
Seven-fifty.

00:30.100 --> 00:32.340
<i>Europol has announced that the explosion</i>

00:32.340 --> 00:35.210
<i>was caused by a malfunctioning 
remote detonation device.</i>

00:35.210 --> 00:37.620
<i>The counterfeit coins implicated in the 
explosion are thought to be the same</i>

00:37.620 --> 00:40.160
<i>as the ones discovered following the 
discovery of the Sky Casino terror plot.</i>

00:40.610 --> 00:42.790
What a tragedy.

00:42.790 --> 00:44.600
Do you happen to have any thoughts?

00:44.600 --> 00:46.200
Only that I agree.

00:46.680 --> 00:49.550
It was the doing of terrorists like you.

00:49.820 --> 00:51.680
The Detective Agency is innocent.

00:52.180 --> 00:53.630
Oh, fine.

00:54.400 --> 00:56.450
I've brought a pear.

00:56.920 --> 00:57.940
Are you giving it to me?

00:58.520 --> 01:00.360
Of course not.

01:00.640 --> 01:05.280
It might not seem like it,
but I admire you.

01:05.680 --> 01:08.740
That day, when you were about 
to blow yourself up mid-air,

01:08.740 --> 01:11.770
you grabbed Tetchou-san 
and used him as a shield

01:11.770 --> 01:13.850
to protect yourself from 
the grenade explosion.

01:16.390 --> 01:21.430
Without that, not even our gifted 
doctors could have saved you.

01:22.380 --> 01:24.970
Your talent is worthy of praise.

01:24.970 --> 01:26.080
So...

01:26.080 --> 01:29.220
I've come up with a way to have 
you alone deemed innocent.

01:29.590 --> 01:32.440
Kunikida-san, would you like 
to join the Hunting Dogs?

01:32.440 --> 01:33.290
What?

01:33.640 --> 01:37.480
Join us in hunting down and arresting 
the Armed Detective Agency.

01:37.480 --> 01:39.740
That's the price for your freedom.

01:40.190 --> 01:43.080
Given that you'd need routine surgery 
each month in order to stay alive,

01:43.080 --> 01:45.030
you'd have no choice but to remain loyal.

01:45.030 --> 01:45.920
Leave.

01:46.280 --> 01:48.580
Do you think I'd betray the Agency?

01:48.580 --> 01:51.950
Unless you accept this offer and the surgery,

01:51.950 --> 01:57.000
you will lose not just your ideals 
but all of your special abilities.

01:57.000 --> 01:58.430
My abilities?

01:58.430 --> 02:00.090
Your notebook.

02:00.400 --> 02:03.760
How would you write without 
either of your hands?

02:08.270 --> 02:10.480
<b>Harukawa 35     Asagiri Kafka</b>

03:34.020 --> 03:35.190
So...

03:35.470 --> 03:36.990
What are you gonna do now?

03:39.230 --> 03:41.810
<i>We have to get the page by 
the day of the full moon.</i>

03:41.810 --> 03:43.980
<i>That's the only way out of this.</i>

03:44.470 --> 03:47.620
<i>But with Sigma dead, we have no leads.</i>

03:48.210 --> 03:51.150
<i>If only we had the rest of the Detective Agency...</i>

03:51.150 --> 03:52.400
<i>This wouldn't have been a big deal.</i>

03:52.400 --> 03:53.410
Don't be clingy.

03:54.230 --> 03:56.580
Find a way with the strength you have now.

04:04.120 --> 04:06.350
Let's look for more clues.

04:07.430 --> 04:09.320
We might have missed something.

04:10.530 --> 04:12.920
I'm sure if we work together,

04:13.680 --> 04:16.910
we'll find some new...

04:19.780 --> 04:20.880
Atsushi-kun!

04:22.990 --> 04:25.330
Now, then, I'll be off.

04:26.010 --> 04:29.790
I'm sure you'll need some 
time to consider my offer.

04:30.780 --> 04:32.670
Oh, right.

04:33.250 --> 04:36.200
The doctor's execution has 
been scheduled for today.

04:37.120 --> 04:42.510
That goes to show that your "ideals" of 
protecting your own kind amount to nothing.

04:44.960 --> 04:47.020
Isn't it about time?

04:45.590 --> 04:46.990
<b>Ideals</b>

05:19.960 --> 05:21.440
You're awake.

05:22.990 --> 05:24.210
Nikolai!

05:25.390 --> 05:26.780
Why are you here?

05:27.620 --> 05:29.410
You're amazing!

05:29.410 --> 05:31.530
Look at how shocked you are.

05:31.530 --> 05:34.090
Amazingly...

05:34.090 --> 05:35.670
plain.

05:37.680 --> 05:39.970
I fell from the Sky Casino...

05:40.430 --> 05:42.100
And I don't have a single scratch.

05:42.780 --> 05:45.430
It's actually a simple magic trick.

05:46.020 --> 05:49.050
I used my spatial splicing ability 
to catch you on your way down

05:49.050 --> 05:51.590
and spit you out in the opposite direction.

05:51.590 --> 05:53.660
I kept doing that until 
you gradually lost speed.

05:53.990 --> 05:59.240
I'm also using my ability to loop 
your blood back into your body.

05:59.540 --> 06:02.660
I practically got blood 
out of a stone for you!

06:03.250 --> 06:04.480
Get it?

06:04.800 --> 06:08.160
I'm certain Fyodor was the one 
who ordered the hit on me.

06:08.650 --> 06:10.770
Why would you save me?

06:11.210 --> 06:14.510
I thought you died in the hostage incident.

06:14.510 --> 06:16.440
Why don't you just ask me?

06:16.440 --> 06:18.270
I'm right here, after all.

06:20.040 --> 06:21.720
How did you survive?

06:21.720 --> 06:24.720
Aww, shucks, I don't know.

06:24.720 --> 06:27.320
Who asks a magician to reveal his tricks?

06:27.320 --> 06:30.790
That's, like, so rude, y'know?

06:31.300 --> 06:32.880
Nah, I kid.

06:32.880 --> 06:34.250
It's a simple trick.

06:34.250 --> 06:38.310
I used my spatial splicing ability to make 
a gap and connect it with another torso.

06:38.310 --> 06:41.390
All the chainsaw did was split that space.

06:41.390 --> 06:43.140
I still don't get it.

06:43.520 --> 06:46.130
If you ever see a magician die 
with their arms and legs tied up,

06:46.130 --> 06:47.830
you have to question the trick.

06:47.830 --> 06:48.860
No.

06:49.740 --> 06:53.210
You're definitely an elite 
Gifted for whom anything goes.

06:54.030 --> 06:56.520
But that's not what I'm surprised about.

06:57.270 --> 07:00.080
In the plan, you were <i>supposed</i> to die.

07:00.470 --> 07:02.650
All in order to erase the 
real culprit from the scene

07:02.650 --> 07:05.700
and force the Agency to go on the run.

07:07.130 --> 07:09.870
You agreed to that plan when you joined.

07:10.900 --> 07:12.650
You're absolutely right.

07:12.930 --> 07:15.250
I was, in fact, intent on dying.

07:15.910 --> 07:19.610
So that I could prove the 
existence of true free will.

07:19.900 --> 07:23.860
I didn't expect anyone else 
to understand that motive.

07:24.610 --> 07:25.580
Alas...

07:27.790 --> 07:29.210
Fantastic.

07:29.680 --> 07:35.680
You resist God and fight to lose yourself.

07:37.020 --> 07:38.670
I was awestruck.

07:38.670 --> 07:40.700
He saw the truth.

07:41.200 --> 07:45.830
Fyodor is the only person who 
understands me. My only friend.

07:46.790 --> 07:48.080
That's what I thought.

07:49.050 --> 07:51.390
And that's when I realized:

07:51.390 --> 07:58.080
If I killed this friend of mine, we would 
be free even from the grip of our emotions.

07:58.080 --> 08:02.290
I could prove that I'm a truly free bird.

08:02.700 --> 08:04.160
<i>This man...</i>

08:04.580 --> 08:06.550
I'll kill Fyodor-kun.

08:07.850 --> 08:15.360
For that, I'd like you to use your ability 
to determine what his special ability is.

08:18.950 --> 08:20.510
He won't come to.

08:21.250 --> 08:25.190
<i>The only cause I can think of is 
the empowered bullet that hit him.</i>

08:28.580 --> 08:31.730
<i>In which case, this is a 
part of Fyodor's scheme.</i>

08:32.220 --> 08:34.670
<i>What might they do in this situation?</i>

08:36.490 --> 08:38.220
<i>Threaten us using the virus special ability,
as they did during the cannibalism?</i>

08:38.220 --> 08:40.640
<i>In other words, Atsushi would be a hostage.</i>

08:41.890 --> 08:45.800
<i>If we hunt down the mastermind,
he would die.</i>

08:46.330 --> 08:49.370
<i>But if we don't stop the terrorism,
millions will die.</i>

08:49.740 --> 08:51.570
<i>As a member of the 
Special Operations Division,</i>

08:51.570 --> 08:53.790
<i>the security of this nation 
is my top priority.</i>

08:54.560 --> 08:56.560
<i>But it isn't for these two.</i>

08:57.020 --> 09:00.600
<i>If they were forced to choose, 
they would choose Atsushi-kun.</i>

09:01.370 --> 09:04.260
<i>I wouldn't stand a chance in a fight.</i>

09:10.410 --> 09:11.470
Atsushi-kun!

09:13.120 --> 09:14.200
Ango-san...

09:15.340 --> 09:17.490
I know where the page is.

09:22.310 --> 09:24.740
Sigma told you where the page is?

09:24.740 --> 09:25.690
Yes.

09:25.690 --> 09:27.220
With his special ability.

09:27.860 --> 09:30.530
I think it happened when he grabbed my hand.

09:30.980 --> 09:31.990
Why?

09:31.990 --> 09:33.220
I don't know.

09:33.940 --> 09:36.100
<i>Because he was betrayed by Fyodor?</i>

09:36.830 --> 09:38.100
<i>Or...</i>

09:39.030 --> 09:42.260
You never knew your reason for being?

09:42.500 --> 09:46.550
Those are words that can never 
be a person's last! It's wrong!

09:47.610 --> 09:50.680
You're a kind man.

09:58.500 --> 09:59.670
I see.

10:00.190 --> 10:03.210
That explains why Atsushi-kun collapsed.

10:03.830 --> 10:07.100
When inundated with an overwhelming amount 
of information through a special ability,

10:07.100 --> 10:11.330
the brain sometimes shuts down 
consciousness to focus on processing.

10:11.830 --> 10:15.810
I've had it happen myself 
because of my own abilities.

10:16.720 --> 10:19.130
So, where's the page?

10:19.620 --> 10:24.840
The page is currently held by the leader 
of the Decay of Angels, Kamui.

10:28.980 --> 10:30.230
Kamui?

10:35.180 --> 10:38.650
Isn't it about time?

10:36.690 --> 10:38.630
<b>Ideals</b>

10:43.290 --> 10:45.110
Snipers through the window!

10:46.610 --> 10:47.580
Dammit...

10:48.370 --> 10:49.240
What?!

10:49.450 --> 10:50.760
They shot the electronic lock!

11:02.390 --> 11:04.160
Who the hell are you?

11:05.460 --> 11:06.690
Kamui.

11:06.980 --> 11:07.790
Shit!

11:10.880 --> 11:14.140
If we defeat him, will it solve the case?

11:15.780 --> 11:17.640
Let's take him down. Ourselves.

11:17.640 --> 11:19.730
And where is he?

11:20.050 --> 11:21.060
About that...

11:21.060 --> 11:23.620
I don't know if it's because 
of the amount of information,

11:23.620 --> 11:25.750
but I can't quite get a 
clear picture in my mind.

11:25.750 --> 11:28.750
Ango-san, is there anything I can do?

11:29.420 --> 11:30.910
Let's see...

11:31.180 --> 11:34.350
This won't solve the underlying problem,
 but an external stimulus can help.

11:34.350 --> 11:38.130
For example, some might process their memories

11:38.130 --> 11:40.500
in response to being stabbed or punched.

11:40.500 --> 11:41.950
Pain...

11:41.950 --> 11:43.380
Like pinching his cheeks?

11:43.380 --> 11:45.970
No, breathe on the back of his neck.

11:45.970 --> 11:48.130
<i>These girls are so protective.</i>

11:49.110 --> 11:51.030
How about this, then.

11:51.030 --> 11:54.620
First, I'll use my ability to 
read Atsushi-kun's information.

11:55.080 --> 11:58.690
Then, if you hurt me,
my memories will be organized, and...

11:58.690 --> 11:59.700
That's it!

11:59.980 --> 12:02.730
I'll have Anne throw you against the wall.

12:02.730 --> 12:04.860
I'll stab you in the calf.

12:04.860 --> 12:06.830
<i>Something about this doesn't 
sit right with me.</i>

12:06.830 --> 12:08.390
Slam him against the floor?

12:08.390 --> 12:09.270
Jab his eyes.

12:09.270 --> 12:10.270
Fling him around!

12:10.270 --> 12:11.010
Kick him.

12:16.470 --> 12:17.690
<i>What was that?</i>

12:17.690 --> 12:19.240
<i>Was it bloodlust?</i>

12:19.800 --> 12:21.300
<i>Someone wants to kill me?</i>

12:22.200 --> 12:23.390
<i>I see...</i>

12:23.820 --> 12:25.720
<i>Kamui's information...</i>

12:26.450 --> 12:29.180
Ango-san, I know where Kamui-san is!

12:29.630 --> 12:32.170
He's in the middle of an assassination!

12:32.760 --> 12:34.940
His target is the Armed Detective Agency.

12:35.430 --> 12:38.390
He's going to wipe out 
each and every member!

12:38.650 --> 12:41.340
<b>807 Explosion Site</b>

12:53.320 --> 12:54.510
What was that?!

12:54.510 --> 12:55.410
Explosion on the road ahead!

12:55.920 --> 12:57.760
<i>It may be an enemy attack.</i>

12:58.250 --> 12:59.870
<i>We'll scout up ahead.</i>

12:59.870 --> 13:01.890
<i>You two watch the rear.</i>

13:01.890 --> 13:02.840
Understood.

13:03.570 --> 13:04.590
We'll be right back.

13:04.860 --> 13:05.990
Don't try to run.

13:10.650 --> 13:12.180
There's no telling what could come for us.

13:12.780 --> 13:14.230
Be on your guard.

13:15.590 --> 13:16.870
Hey, Sergeant.

13:16.870 --> 13:18.030
Where's the doctor?

13:20.640 --> 13:22.570
The doctor's missing...

13:22.570 --> 13:23.720
Along with the car.

13:28.060 --> 13:29.270
Hey, mister guard?

13:29.510 --> 13:33.650
I have a life-threatening illness that means 
I die if I don't have my electronics.

13:33.650 --> 13:36.540
Could I at least have my phone back?

13:38.630 --> 13:39.940
No?

13:40.470 --> 13:41.810
Oh, fine.

13:47.000 --> 13:49.700
I want to help the Armed Detective Agency,

13:49.700 --> 13:53.330
but they won't even let me out of my 
own home because I'm a former member.

13:58.210 --> 13:59.250
It's...

13:59.250 --> 14:01.100
A cellular terminal!

14:01.100 --> 14:03.540
I can reach the outside!

14:13.440 --> 14:14.790
Fukuzawa, get out.

14:16.830 --> 14:19.260
We'll be in charge of your 
interrogation going forward.

14:19.800 --> 14:21.080
Put this on.

14:34.830 --> 14:35.870
I see.

14:36.430 --> 14:40.980
You're going to throw me off 
this building to silence me.

14:43.340 --> 14:45.780
I know who you are.

14:46.570 --> 14:48.190
I know you.

14:48.880 --> 14:51.720
The number you're thinking of...

14:51.720 --> 14:55.020
is 381,882, right?

14:55.020 --> 14:56.260
Correct.

14:56.690 --> 14:59.170
Your number is...

14:59.170 --> 15:02.460
790,115?

15:02.730 --> 15:03.920
This sucks.

15:03.920 --> 15:06.410
The number guessing game is too easy.

15:06.410 --> 15:08.090
Are you all right?

15:08.360 --> 15:09.560
About what?

15:09.560 --> 15:12.230
I'm worried for the Detective Agency.

15:12.230 --> 15:15.820
The Detective Agency was 
defeated at the Sky Casino.

15:15.820 --> 15:18.670
Isn't there something you need to be doing?

15:19.340 --> 15:21.740
I'm bored over here.

15:21.740 --> 15:22.820
More so than you.

15:23.220 --> 15:25.940
Keeping an eye on you is about all I can do.

15:25.940 --> 15:29.880
And as long as I'm doing that,
he can move freely.

15:29.880 --> 15:31.080
Who can?

15:31.560 --> 15:33.690
Isn't it obvious?

15:34.130 --> 15:37.090
The superhuman exceeding even the Gifted.

15:37.090 --> 15:39.530
The strongest man in the Detective Agency.

15:40.040 --> 15:43.040
<b>Episode 51
The Strongest Man</b>

15:43.970 --> 15:46.200
Boss successfully extracted!

15:46.570 --> 15:49.860
Man, sorry we had to be so rough.

15:49.860 --> 15:52.300
Better than the other members, though.

15:52.720 --> 15:54.840
They're after the others, too, huh?

15:55.340 --> 15:58.300
Kamui's hand was devilishly sharp and swift.

15:58.300 --> 16:03.260
So to save time, I took the liberty of 
taking over his assassination plot.

16:03.930 --> 16:08.340
Long story short, the members who 
were being targeted are all safe.

16:08.340 --> 16:12.340
But, Rampo... I was told that you 
were shot when this all began,

16:12.340 --> 16:14.240
and that you had gone missing.

16:14.780 --> 16:18.020
There's only one possible 
reason I'd ever be in danger.

16:18.440 --> 16:22.180
And that's because it's more convenient 
for us if the enemy thinks I'm in danger.

16:23.090 --> 16:25.100
During the hostage situation,

16:25.100 --> 16:28.290
I was surrounded by police as 
part of the enemy conspiracy.

16:35.750 --> 16:38.010
Whoops, my bad.

16:38.360 --> 16:40.860
By the way, nice cape you've got there.

16:40.860 --> 16:42.320
Lemme borrow it for a bit.

16:46.370 --> 16:48.710
Until I feel like giving it back.

16:49.360 --> 16:54.590
I used the chaos of the initial 
investigation to escape their perimeter.

16:54.590 --> 16:55.540
I see.

16:57.460 --> 16:59.730
And then what did you do?

16:59.730 --> 17:01.900
I'm an elite detective.

17:01.900 --> 17:04.620
There's only one thing an 
elite detective ever does.

17:04.620 --> 17:06.420
Solve crimes.

17:07.120 --> 17:11.120
I figured out the assassination 
plot as part of my investigation,

17:11.120 --> 17:15.080
but to save all of our members, 
I needed more time to prepare.

17:15.080 --> 17:18.460
So I decided to rewrite 
the enemy's plan instead.

17:20.420 --> 17:23.020
The sniper rifle that was meant
 to take out Kunikida

17:24.290 --> 17:25.910
destroyed the electronic lock instead.

17:26.390 --> 17:29.450
I used knockout gas to get Kunikida out.

17:35.920 --> 17:39.610
For Yosano-san's rescue,
I rigged the prison vehicle ahead of time.

17:40.470 --> 17:43.110
I swapped the engine out 
with an electric one.

17:43.450 --> 17:46.370
Electric motors make almost no noise.

17:46.700 --> 17:50.510
And as long as it's playing 
fake engine noises,

17:50.510 --> 17:52.770
no one notices the engine's 
been swapped out.

17:53.210 --> 17:56.750
The attacker had been planning to blow up 
the vehicle with a remote-controlled mine.

17:56.980 --> 17:59.910
I took the controller and set it off early.

18:03.460 --> 18:07.070
Of the four soldiers, two were 
ordered to investigate ahead,

18:07.070 --> 18:09.800
and the other two stood guard behind.

18:09.800 --> 18:11.680
No one was watching the vehicle.

18:12.130 --> 18:13.300
And then...

18:13.820 --> 18:17.640
I used a mirror to hide 
myself and get in the car.

18:17.640 --> 18:18.620
After that,

18:19.670 --> 18:24.350
I turned off the engine noise and 
quietly drove away onto a side-road.

18:25.170 --> 18:27.710
That's the trick behind Yosano-san's rescue.

18:28.160 --> 18:31.670
Now, lastly, how we saved Katai...

18:31.670 --> 18:33.470
This one was simple.

18:33.470 --> 18:35.210
I used an accomplice.

18:35.210 --> 18:36.580
An accomplice?

18:36.580 --> 18:37.690
Yup!

18:37.690 --> 18:39.370
It is I!

18:39.370 --> 18:43.720
We displayed a novel Poe-kun 
wrote on the phone screen

18:47.980 --> 18:51.230
and took him into the novel world, 
where he would be safe.

18:53.100 --> 18:56.470
I was also responsible for the sniping 
and for preparing the vehicle.

18:56.470 --> 18:57.610
I was a huge asset!

18:57.610 --> 18:59.410
We don't have time for 
your gloating right now.

18:59.410 --> 19:00.550
Maybe next time.

19:00.940 --> 19:02.690
So anyway...

19:02.690 --> 19:04.480
Everyone's waiting for the boss' orders.

19:05.350 --> 19:07.370
Then I shall issue an order.

19:08.470 --> 19:10.140
Shut this damn plot down!

19:12.160 --> 19:13.940
That's what I was hoping to hear.

19:16.920 --> 19:19.590
Is anyone going to watch this 
stupid press conference?

19:19.890 --> 19:23.370
It's about the son of the KS Company's 
president and his suspected affair.

19:23.370 --> 19:25.560
It's the talk of the town.

19:25.560 --> 19:27.350
Who gives a damn?

19:27.690 --> 19:29.620
Look at the state of the world!

19:30.340 --> 19:32.600
Reporters around the world are freaking out

19:32.600 --> 19:34.560
about the Armed Detective 
Agency's terrorist attack.

19:35.350 --> 19:37.780
The UN even says it's going to create

19:37.780 --> 19:40.810
a counter-terrorism unit
in response to the incident.

19:40.810 --> 19:42.320
What's your point?

19:42.320 --> 19:44.160
I noticed something.

19:44.410 --> 19:47.610
Of all the ceaseless coverage 
of the Detective Agency,

19:47.610 --> 19:49.790
there's one mystery that 
they aren't bringing up.

19:49.790 --> 19:50.800
And what's that?

19:50.800 --> 19:52.420
Their motive.

19:52.420 --> 19:53.740
The biggest mystery.

19:53.740 --> 19:55.210
The reason for their attacks.

19:55.210 --> 19:58.660
We have to get these criminals to fess up,
and bring it to the public!

19:58.660 --> 20:02.480
Isn't that the whole reason 
we became journos?!

20:06.770 --> 20:10.220
Hey, do they not serve tea at these events?

20:10.680 --> 20:12.230
T-T-T...

20:12.570 --> 20:14.220
Terrorist!

20:14.480 --> 20:16.650
<b>Municipal Police Headquarters</b>

20:15.250 --> 20:16.640
Everyone, check the TV!

20:16.880 --> 20:18.260
A live broadcast?

20:18.260 --> 20:19.160
That's near here!

20:19.160 --> 20:21.430
Why is the suspect doing this?

20:21.790 --> 20:23.320
The doors won't open!

20:23.320 --> 20:24.940
Are we hostages?!

20:25.230 --> 20:27.350
Come on. Let's get out of here.

20:28.090 --> 20:30.840
What is the reason behind 
your terror attacks?!

20:31.560 --> 20:33.120
Excellent question.

20:37.930 --> 20:39.030
<i>Huy!</i>

20:39.030 --> 20:40.680
<i>What's upsy-daisy!</i>

20:40.680 --> 20:42.850
<i>So, Armed Detective Agency...</i>

20:44.150 --> 20:46.090
This is the message was delivered

20:46.090 --> 20:48.170
to the Detective Agency six afternoons ago.

20:48.960 --> 20:51.360
Now, what happened after this?

20:51.680 --> 20:53.560
As I'm sure you're aware...

20:54.100 --> 20:55.370
This happened.

21:00.870 --> 21:03.150
And the Detective Agency, 
who was there to help,

21:03.150 --> 21:06.130
was instead made out to be terrorists.

21:06.130 --> 21:08.250
Are you making excuses now?

21:08.250 --> 21:11.070
Cut it out! He'll kill us!

21:11.070 --> 21:12.960
Or do you have proof that you're innocent?

21:13.350 --> 21:14.930
I have proof.

21:14.930 --> 21:15.820
Right here.

21:16.690 --> 21:20.590
This morning, I sent a copy of this 
to every law enforcement agency.

21:20.870 --> 21:22.930
<i>Fingerprints and hair lifted from the site.</i>

21:23.220 --> 21:24.860
<i>Changes in the hostage plans.</i>

21:24.860 --> 21:26.820
<i>Transaction records for the chainsaw.</i>

21:27.480 --> 21:32.320
<i>Evidence that contradicts the supposition 
that the Agency was behind the terror attack.</i>

21:32.320 --> 21:34.110
<i>And evidence that should exist but doesn't.</i>

21:34.680 --> 21:36.710
I've documented all of it.

21:38.330 --> 21:39.390
Want one?

21:39.390 --> 21:42.120
You! Where's that envelope?!

21:42.390 --> 21:43.970
D-Dunno.

21:48.830 --> 21:49.750
Here.

21:50.200 --> 21:52.850
Why is it in the garbage unopened?!

21:53.900 --> 21:58.390
The power of the page has made it so that 
no one believes in the Agency's innocence.

21:58.890 --> 22:00.220
The page?

22:00.220 --> 22:04.950
The page is a special sheet of paper 
that has the ability to amend reality.

22:06.020 --> 22:08.910
Everything written on 
that page becomes true.

22:09.280 --> 22:11.000
The actual attackers
have written on the page

22:11.000 --> 22:15.940
"The Armed Detective Agency is behind 
the Decay of Angels case."

22:16.170 --> 22:18.590
"Law enforcement organizations"

22:18.590 --> 22:22.610
"do not question the fact that the 
Armed Detective Agency is guilty."

22:22.610 --> 22:24.740
The documents are probably 
in the trash about now.

22:28.840 --> 22:32.090
Okay, it should be about time now.

22:35.280 --> 22:36.860
Everyone, hold still!

22:42.480 --> 22:44.310
I'll be off now.

22:45.010 --> 22:47.630
I want to say this to anyone in 
the police who are watching:

22:48.350 --> 22:50.590
Don't think about it based
on your "position" or "job."

22:51.020 --> 22:53.090
Think with your soul.

22:57.760 --> 23:00.440
Think? About what?

23:00.950 --> 23:02.400
Twelve years.

23:03.040 --> 23:07.600
In the past twelve years,
I've solved tens of thousands of cases.

23:07.890 --> 23:12.270
There are several officers in
 this room whose lives I've saved.

23:13.600 --> 23:14.120
Right?

23:16.100 --> 23:17.210
Think!

23:18.120 --> 23:20.750
If this excellent detective 
is a terrorist mastermind,

23:21.270 --> 23:26.000
would he be so stupid as to put 
himself on the wanted list?

23:27.020 --> 23:31.290
<i>Look with your own eyes, 
and it should be obvious:</i>

23:31.580 --> 23:36.020
It's actually quite easy to 
become an excellent detective.

23:36.050 --> 23:40.050
Next Episode: Episode 52

23:36.050 --> 23:40.050
<i>The Answer to Everything</i>
